# Homebrew bundle -- everything in this image that no Fedora repository carries.
#
# `brew bundle --file=/usr/share/homebrew/Brewfile` installs all of it, and
# neutronos-brew-bundle.service does exactly that, once, on first boot. Add a tool
# here rather than reaching for a third-party RPM repo.
#
# Two rules, both learned the hard way by a broken build:
#   1. Only what Fedora does not package. Anything Fedora has belongs in the
#      recipe's rpm-ostree module, where it gets security updates from Fedora
#      instead of from whatever a brew tap happens to build.
#   2. Nothing that needs root, setuid, or a daemon. Homebrew refuses to run as
#      root, so this is a per-user tool list and nothing more.
#
# `brew install <formula>` still works and is the right answer for anything only
# you want; this file is for what the image should always have.

# A git TUI. Not packaged for Fedora at all -- same reason Ghostty is not -- and
# it used to be a build-breaking `lazygit` line in the recipe until it moved here.
brew "lazygit"